      {q:'Which planet is farthest from the Sun?', o:['Uranus','Saturn','Pluto','Neptune'], c:3, e:'Neptune — 4.5 billion km away. Pluto is a dwarf planet, not a planet!'},
      {q:'Between which planets is the asteroid belt?', o:['Earth and Mars','Mars and Jupiter','Jupiter and Saturn','Venus and Earth'], c:1, e:'Between Mars and Jupiter — millions of rocky fragments circle there.'},
      {q:'After the Moon, what is the brightest object in the night sky?', o:['Mars','Venus','Sirius','Jupiter'], c:1, e:'Venus! Its thick clouds reflect sunlight strongly — the «morning star».'},
      {q:'Who was the first person to walk on the Moon?', o:['Yuri Gagarin','Neil Armstrong','Buzz Aldrin','Alan Shepard'], c:1, e:'Neil Armstrong — July 20, 1969, Apollo 11 mission.'},
      {q:'How long does Earth take to spin once on its axis?', o:['12 hours','24 hours','7 days','365 days'], c:1, e:'24 hours — that is why day and night alternate.'},
      {q:'Which is the smallest planet in the Solar System?', o:['Mars','Venus','Mercury','Pluto'], c:2, e:'Mercury — 4,880 km across, about a third of Earth. Pluto is not a planet!'},
      {q:'What element is the Sun mostly made of?', o:['Oxygen','Hydrogen','Iron','Carbon'], c:1, e:'Hydrogen (~74%)! In the core it fuses into helium, releasing enormous energy.'},
      {q:'How many moons does Mars have?', o:['0','1','2','4'], c:2, e:'Two — Phobos and Deimos. Both are tiny and potato-shaped.'},
      {q:'Why does a comet grow a tail?', o:['It flies very fast','The Sun evaporates its ice','It is burning','Because of wind'], c:1, e:'Near the Sun its ice evaporates into a gas-dust tail — always pointing away from the Sun.'},
      {q:'How long does Earth take to orbit the Sun?', o:['30 days','180 days','365 days','730 days'], c:2, e:'365 days (365.25 exactly — those quarters add up to a leap day every 4 years).'}
